      '<p>Pinui binui (evacuation and construction) is the Israeli urban renewal track in which old residential buildings in a declared complex are demolished and replaced by new ones. Owners sell their old rights to a developer and receive a new apartment in the project, rent for the building years and guarantees, without paying for the construction. A complex has at least 24 existing units and, after building, at least 70 units or double, whichever is higher.</p>\n'
